   119	# override that the rail enforcing in every mode never saw.
   120	#
   121	# The semantics chosen for BOTH rails, and the reason: NON-CANONICAL
   122	# top-level syntax is REJECTED, fail-closed. Trimming the key in both
   123	# readers would also close the divergence, but it widens the grammar of a
   124	# SIGNED artifact to shapes no author writes and no template emits — every
   125	# new accepted spelling is another chance for the next reader to disagree.
